+# Task 2 core milestone: continuation map
+
+All 168 full acceptance points remain incomplete pending independent audit. Focused passing observations do not mark whole AUTH groups passed. Continue within the authorized isolated spike, not formal B1.
+
+| Missing path / exact boundary | Existing public contract and stored data | Minimum continuation |
+|---|---|---|
+| Knowledge browse/maintain/distribute/download, locked inheritance/custom browse, parent append, import, classroom subject, published state | Task1 `normalizeCatalog`, `assertGrantSubset`, `SubjectResolvers`; `knowledge.category` currently hierarchy IDs only | Add tenant-bound category grant/ancestry lock/course/subject tables and owning public facts port. Normalize effective ancestry centrally, feed grants to bulk candidate/compiler, add separate actions and publication facts, persist mutation under authority revision lock. Test every API/import/creator bypass and independent download path. |
+| Delegation create/edit, selected membership ceilings, recheck/cycle, source caps audit | Task1 `assertCanDelegate`, `assertGrantSubset`, `ObjectSet`; `authz.membership.data/source_id`; `OrganizationService.revoke` freezes descendants; org mutations conservatively freeze all derived memberships | Add domain service to enumerate true business objects by node/anchor using module ports, compare selected membership only, persist frozen cap snapshot/revision/dependencies. Reject graph cycles, explicitly recheck to active/suspended, include raw-field caps and membership reincarnation. No HTTP grant DTO should be mistaken for trusted normalized grants. |
+| Team enrollment add/remove | Task1 `teamMembers`; OrganizationPort central scope resolver; `training.project.team_enabled`, `training.roster`; TrainingService.save persists switch | Register exact team actions and server-owned role/appointment capability distinction. Resolve direct-manager IDs in one public bulk call; require action + team switch only for team source, current target state/company cap, and all affected company caps for whole commands. Test M's A/B vs C/D/E and appointment unaffected. |
+| Own-wallet/account exception and company offsets/references | Task1 ownWallet hard constraint requires person=actor, nonempty authoritative dataCompanyId, crossCompanyReference=false; compiler has matching fields | Add account-owned company partitions/balance/debt/reference fixture tables and scoped account service. Separate own read from management/report scopes; enforce no cross-company offsets/reference links. No account path currently exists. |
+| Company grant mutations and current-state propagation fidelity | `authz.company_grant`, trigger-backed revision; `OrganizationService.update` and `report.person_projection`; history has immutable data_company_id | Add centralized grant/revoke command with selected capability and dependency freezing. Add strong owner-to-report projection public delivery port; current implementation writes projection in same org command transaction, not an outbox. Test transfer, disable/delete/restore, current report filters vs acting account validity, historical snapshots unchanged and company grant preservation. |
+| Company-bound project attachments/progress/search/export, ordinary shared content learner | `training.project` shared content, roster has data company; TrainingService.projects/roster/media; existing ExportService is **report only** | Add owning attachment/progress tables and company-bound node/action mapping. Shared project content must stay tenant-level even with internal creator. Use company-bound predicates for roster/count/search/progress/attachments; separate project export create/execute/claim with frozen scope and revision. Current media is a synthetic shared project segment only, not a company attachment or course publication proof. |
+| Full matrix and data edges | Existing literal fixtures, 50k/500/2000/20 roles/1m facts, report field projection, same-source SQL | Add same-name cross-tenant fixture (currently IDs only), historical job/status snapshots, current-state history tests, null dept/manager clearing, all six-scope empty/unsupported mutations, raw log/cache/denial scans, direct domain/jobs, field/node/action coupled negatives, membership regrant overrides. Existing populated subtree moves fail closed rather than implementing a general validated move. |
+| Export reliability/large output | report.export_job; create/execute/claim central checks | Replace single-transaction in-memory accumulation with protected chunked output and durable limited service identity. Each page currently reauthorizes in one transaction; no per-row N+1, but repeated page permission work and memory footprint remain unsuitable as production design. Creation/execute/claim reject any changed tenant revision (safe, conservative over-invalidation). |
+| Measurement/revocation completion | benchmark.ts, run-faults.ts, real race tests and gzip samples | Add cold Redis fault, export execute/claim fault and revoke timing, batch delegation/download races. Warm Redis disconnect/timeout/reconnect, DB failure, B next media after A revoke and two lock orderings are focused real evidence. Record commit timestamps precisely from transaction boundary/audit, not only HTTP completion as an upper bound. Then run capped50client600s windows per scenario/candidate/cache and browser QA. |
+
+## Static table access map / splitability
+
+- `report/service.ts` reads only `report.person_projection` and `report.learning_fact`; the SQL compiler emits bound `unnest` person relations and never joins organization tables.
+- `report/exports.ts` reads/writes only `report.export_job` and calls ReportService. It never calls the object candidate per row.
+- `organization/public.ts` owns private department/person scope reads; it uses central `resolveScope` semantics first against representative departments, then retrieves relevant people in one query. ALL and SELF skip enumeration.
+- `authz/revision.ts` is the trusted central facts adapter and currently reads organization person plus authz revision/company_grant/session/membership and training appointment directly. Its queries should be moved behind explicit OrganizationFacts/TrainingFacts public ports before module splitting; this milestone does not claim a mechanically separable build.
+- `organization/service.ts` owns person mutations but currently writes report projection and reads authz membership/revision via central services. Replace the projection SQL with a ReportProjection public application port, while retaining one database transaction or an independently proved revision-consistent projection protocol.
+- `training/service.ts` owns project/roster/appointment SQL but currently reads person company directly for appointment target validation. Move that read to OrganizationPublic before enforcing static boundaries.
+- Schema tenant-qualified FKs protect organization company/department/person, role memberships, appointments, rosters, report learning-to-current-person projection and export ownership. A full per-module DB-role privilege split and RLS are not implemented.
+
+## Evidence limitations
+
+Initial RED outputs prove missing integration module / absent HTTP server, not a RED for each later positive fixture. SQL and HTTP were run against real infrastructure. Expanded six-scope and concurrency tests were added after the first implementation to audit those behaviors; the report must not mislabel them as independent pre-implementation RED. Controller-required complete TDD record is therefore partial at this milestone. Correct the verification process for subsequent additions rather than manufacturing historic RED output.
